Loading and startup **pass** on the current build at http://localhost:8000. I found no blocking defects and nothing new for the coders.

**What I checked:**
- **Right build being served:** nothing was running on port 8000, so I started a server on `dist/` and confirmed it was serving this project's page. The build is up to date (`make -n` had nothing to do), and the source matches the version the tester and coder reports used.
- **Fresh load with the browser cache cleared:** the page and all its files, including the game code and game data, came back OK. No requests failed, there were no page errors, and the console had no errors.
- **Startup:** the first frame drew at about 208 ms. The game ran at 34.8 tics/s overall and 33.1/s in the first half-second. The target is about 35, so this resolves the earlier report's open item that the first-seconds rate was never measured.
- **Picture and colours:** I looked at the screenshots. The title screen and the demo that plays after it have correct colours (no red/blue swap), and the picture keeps its shape with black bars at the sides.
- **Responsiveness:** pressing Escape opens the main menu.
- **Smaller window:** at 800×600 the picture still keeps its shape and there are no scrollbars.
- **Console warnings:** two per load, both the browser blocking audio until the user clicks or presses a key, which is expected. A third warning came from my own pixel sampling, not the game.

